1
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The local app (uv run afs-assist ui): type an enquiry, try an example, or open a finished one.

2
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,000
A new, generic enquiry: ethanol in a clear, filtered fermentation broth in a pipe; GC is the lab reference.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Get assessment: the real pipeline starts (production models, live literature search).

4
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Pipeline steps with timings: read the enquiry, screen methods against the AFS rules, assess.

5
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Live activity feed: methods ruled out with the S01 Table 1 reason; 29 citations checked against the AFS pages.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:53,000
One hard check failed, so the failed checks go back to the model for a repair round.

7
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Answer after 107 s (pipeline wall time, $0.036): the recommendation, a pinned strip (status, confidence, open questions), quotes in the margin.

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Status, confidence with its reason, and the next step. Every quote beside the answer is word for word from AFS.

9
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Open a margin quote: the stored S01 p.18 page text with the quote highlighted, marked verified (exact match).

10
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Options: simple, recommended, extended. Cost class comes from S01 Table 1 (p.6) rows; it is not a price.

11
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Setup sketch drawn by code from the proposed option; the dashed sensor is auxiliary, to be confirmed with AFS.

12
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,000
A follow-up in the composer: "Why not Raman as the first choice?"

13
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Follow-up questions are answered from the assessment and the AFS pages: one model call, quotes checked before display.

14
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Answer in 5.3 s, $0.006: each point cited (S01 p.18, p.11, p.6), or marked as engineering judgement.

15
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Inline result blocks: the setup sketch of the Raman (simple) option and the first feasibility test.

16
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Answer an open question in place: process temperature about 32 °C, 28 to 36 °C during a batch.

17
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Update the recommendation: the full assessment runs again with the new fact (v2).

18
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:20,000
v2 after 147 s ($0.046): the temperature range is now part of the advice; the open questions drop to Q1 and Q3.

19
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:34,000
What changed, v1 to v2: the method now adds a Raman probe; status and confidence unchanged. A temperature alone does not justify that: a re-assessment is a fresh model run and can shift (a known limitation).
